# Protections for the subprocess-injection variant corpus. Held IDENTICAL across
# every target in this family, and deliberately set to the FULL modern set:
#
# -fstack-protector-strong -pie -fPIE -Wl,-z,relro,-z,now
#
# The point of choosing maximum hardening is that it changes nothing here. This
# category is orthogonal to memory-safety mitigations: there is no overflow, no
# corrupted pointer and no return address involved, so a canary, PIE, NX and Full
# RELRO are all satisfied and the target is still trivially exploitable. A reader
# who sees "all protections on" in the corpus table must not read that as
# "hardened against this".
#
# -O0 keeps the sink call and the filter (where a target has one) visible as
# separate, recognisable instructions so the analysis has something to derive.
-fstack-protector-strong
-pie
-fPIE
-O0
-Wl,-z,relro,-z,now
